  "baseCommit": "67ae27dd2cde879b30982307731240ab0187a081",
  "scope": "Four actual packed SDK source-free arm64 Release gates. Each test-only native toolbar retires the real SDK renderer on the pause/inactive callback caused by an actual OS geolocation permission dialog. Native session listeners are captured at zero before the new renderer registers. The OS grant remains effective in the original Tauri plugin. The retired renderer continuation must not save its sentinel note; the new renderer observes zero notes, then saves exactly one real location note. Original state/setup, events, background deep links, later replacement and removal remain verified. This observes absence of the old saved-note side effect, not a direct count of retired JavaScript callbacks. iOS denial-to-grant explicitly resets privacy and relaunches; the permission-retirement/grant/background/replacement/removal sequence retains one process. A second clean-installed app per gate uses the unmodified generated startup/default layout, with no native acceptance class. Both sessions and original Tauri capabilities remain enforced.",
  "sessionOpenErrors": {
    "code": "caller_denied",
    "message": "Native caller is not declared by this artifact",
    "scope": "Actual SDK rejection in acceptance and default generated apps on both platforms. Current iOS exports preserve the complete ABI response in NSError.userInfo[TauriNativeRuntimeResponse]; older artifacts retain the documented runtime_error fallback. Android already forwards the original ABI response. The C ABI version remains 3."
  },
